  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Card Casting (Cooldown, Mana Pool, Mana Graveyard)</p>\n<p><strong>Benefits:</strong> You may play a magic effect card from your hand as if it were a Mana Point Card. The effect card counts as a number of Mana Point Cards equal to the number of spell points required to play the magic effect card normally. The card is not discarded until all of the spell points it provides are spent or until the end of your turn, whichever comes first. When you would shuffle effect cards played as Mana Point Cards into your deck, you may instead choose to put them on the bottom of your deck in the order that the cards were played.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/card-and-deck-feats#toc15\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
